# Response headers for cindrasec.com.
#
# GitHub Pages cannot set custom HTTP headers, so this file is not applied by
# Pages itself. It serves two purposes:
#   1. The canonical reference for the headers that MUST be configured at the
#      edge — in Cloudflare, via Rules -> Transform Rules -> Modify Response
#      Header (or a Snippet), mirroring every header below.
#   2. Drop-in support if the site ever moves to a host that reads _headers
#      natively (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify).
#
# The CSP <meta> tag in index.html provides in-page enforcement today, but
# frame-ancestors, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options and Permissions-Policy only
# work as real HTTP headers — set them at the edge.
#
# ON style-src 'unsafe-inline' BELOW — it is deliberate, not drift.
# This policy applies to /*, and 404.html carries its CSS in an inline <style>
# block so an error page costs exactly one request no matter which missing URL
# produced it. The pages that matter are stricter than this header: index.html
# and bn/index.html each ship a <meta> CSP with `style-src 'self'`, and a browser
# enforces every policy it receives, so the effective rule on those pages is the
# intersection — 'self' only, no inline styles. Tightening the header here would
# not harden them further; it would only leave the 404 page unstyled.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
